Description: Gate cuse_client.c chmod on file presence (nodoc-safe)
 With DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc set, dh_installexamples skips installing
 the upstream examples into debian/libfuse3-dev/usr/share/doc/libfuse3-dev/
 examples/.  override_dh_fixperms then fails because it unconditionally
 chmods cuse_client.c regardless of whether it was actually staged:
 .
   chmod a-x debian/libfuse3-dev/usr/share/doc/libfuse3-dev/examples/cuse_client.c
   chmod: cannot access '...': No such file or directory
   make[1]: *** [debian/rules:31: override_dh_fixperms] Error 1
 .
 Wrap the chmod in `if [ -f ... ]` so the rule is a no-op when the
 examples directory wasn't populated.  Both the nodoc profile (Athena's
 default per [Source] BuildProfiles in build.conf) and full builds (no
 profiles) work unchanged.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-10
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ override_dh_compress:

 override_dh_fixperms:
 	dh_fixperms
-	chmod a-x debian/libfuse3-dev/usr/share/doc/libfuse3-dev/examples/cuse_client.c
+	if [ -f debian/libfuse3-dev/usr/share/doc/libfuse3-dev/examples/cuse_client.c ]; then chmod a-x debian/libfuse3-dev/usr/share/doc/libfuse3-dev/examples/cuse_client.c; fi

 ifeq ($(DEB_BUILD_ARCH),linux)
 	chmod 0755 debian/fuse3/bin/fusermount3
